The window model, as kdos-comp implements it today.

This is the contract libkwm is written against. Every row here was derived by
reading a named line of compositor source, never by taste: adoption of libkwm is
a behaviour change only where a row says the old behaviour was wrong.

Three sections, because the compositor keeps them in three places:

  tile   the tiled-state transition   src/view.c view_snap_to_edge()
  geom   a tiled state becomes a rect src/view.c view_get_edge_snap_box()
  place  where a new window lands     src/placement.c placement_find_best()

Read geometry.txt with it. A row that cannot be traced to a line does not belong
in the file.
